abstract: >-
  Nexus-MCP is a local MCP server that lets an AI coding agent read less code
  to find the right file. It combines hybrid search (vector + BM25), a static
  code graph with call edges and an opt-in project memory in a single
  process. It provides 8 tools for AI coding agents via the Model Context
  Protocol. The tools aim at fewer agent turns and tokens for the same
  answers. It uses about 90 MB of RAM idle and 270 MB with the
  embedding model loaded, needs no API keys and has no cloud dependencies.
